Like the core scripts, I've used
Graphics.width * scale - window.innerWidth
(and similar for height):
getScaledSize
->
updateScale
. The only difference I can see in that area is that I've used
>> 1
for integer division by 2, instead of
/ 2
like the core scripts. Not sure how that could result in what you describe, though.
I also just realised that my screen bounds check ignores DPI scaling and work area restrictions (e.g. space occupied by taskbar). So you may want to try replacing this line:
JavaScript:
const { width, height } = require("nw.gui").Screen.screens[0].bounds;
...with (something like) this:
JavaScript:
const screen = require("nw.gui").Screen.screens[0];
let { width, height } = screen.work_area;
width /= screen.scaleFactor;
height /= screen.scaleFactor;

